From 3221f5555a1702d53902843f451d7f6d210e9240 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomeu Vizoso <tomeu.vizoso@collabora.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 13:28:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/37] etnaviv/ml: use heap allocations during compilation,
 defer BO creation to submission

Stop allocating kernel driver buffer objects (etna_bo, pipe_resource) during
subgraph compilation. Instead, all data produced during compilation is stored
in plain heap memory (calloc/malloc/free).

A new prepare_submission() function, called lazily from
etna_ml_subgraph_invoke on the first invocation, creates the actual BOs and
uploads the heap data. A relocation mechanism tracks which words in config
data contain GPU addresses that need patching at submission time.

This follows the same pattern used by the ethosu driver, where
ethosu_ml_subgraph_create only allocates heap memory and
prepare_for_submission() creates the DRM/pipe resources at invoke time.
